# PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0

<https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>

## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree
to all of the following terms:

* You may use the Work only for Noncommercial Purposes.
* You may use the Work for Commercial Purposes only if You
  receive a separate written license from the Licensor.

## Commercial Use

A "Commercial Use" means any use of the Work, in whole or in part, that
is primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or
private monetary compensation. Commercial Use includes, without
limitation:

1. Selling the Work, or a product or service that includes the Work
   or a substantial portion of it;
2. Hosting the Work, or a service based on the Work, as a paid
   service, including as part of a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS),
   Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS), or Infrastructure-as-a-Service (IaaS)
   offering;
3. Using the Work in the development or operation of any product
   or service that is sold, licensed, or otherwise provided for a fee,
   including any educational technology product or service;
4. Using the Work to provide paid tutoring, teaching, or
   educational services;
5. Using the Work in connection with advertising or marketing
   activities that generate revenue;
6. Using the Work for internal purposes where the primary purpose
   of the use is to support commercial activity or to reduce
   the cost of commercial activity.

The above list is non-exhaustive.

## Noncommercial Purposes

"Noncommercial Purposes" means use of the Work:

1. By an individual for personal, educational, or recreational
   purposes that are not intended to generate revenue;
2. By a non-profit organization (as recognized by the applicable
   jurisdiction) for its own internal activities;
3. By an educational institution (such as a school, college, or
   university) for non-commercial teaching or research;
4. For research purposes, including academic research, where the
   results are made publicly available;
5. For evaluation, testing, or development purposes by a
   prospective licensee that is considering a commercial license;
6. For open-source contributions back to the project.

The above list is non-exhaustive.

